<div class="row">
<div class="this-term col-sm-12">
  <div class="pref-label">natural resources</div>
  <div class="scope-note">Stocks of anything naturally occurring that have a beneficial use for man including economic, nutritional, recreational, aesthetic, and other benefits.</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="row mb-4">
<div class="col-sm-12">
  <div class="col-sm-8"><b>Subtopics</b><br/><a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=799" title="Natural resources that are used for heat and power generation, including oil, natural gas, coal, and geothermal energy.">energy resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=391" title="The stock of anadromous, marine, and freshwater fish in fishing areas of commercial, subsistence, and recreational value.">fishery resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=411" title="Trees and associated vegetation available for human use.  Use for timber and other forest resources with economic value.">forest resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=745" title="Natural occurrences of useful inorganic elements or compounds.">mineral resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1080" title="Natural resources of unconsolidated fragmented rock, humus, and mineral matter that cover the surface of the earth.">soil resources</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=1308" title="Stocks of water, the liquid derived from precipitation. A constituent of living matter and necessity for all life, it covers a large proportion of the earth&#039;s surface.">water resources</a><br/>
</div>
  <div class="col-sm-4"><b>See also</b><br/><a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=291" title="Broad term for all science related to the study of the earth.">earth sciences</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=650" title="Branches of science that study living and fossil organisms.">life sciences</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=776" title="Using a combination of techniques to control or direct the use of resources and limit population size to reach a predetermined goal, such as sustainability.">natural resource management</a><br/>
<a href="/thesaurus/term-simple.php?thcode=2&amp;code=2280" title="Terrestrial and marine areas that are designated and managed for the preservation of biological diversity or other natural, recreational, or cultural uses.">protected areas</a><br/>
</div>
</div>
